==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From a satirical obituary published in an English newspaper after its loss to [[Australia]] in 1882, announcing the death of English cricket and that "the body would be cremated and the ashes taken to Australia".

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-the Ashes.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|head=[[the]] [[ash|Ashes]]}}

# {{lb|en|cricket}} A [[trophy]] played for by England and Australia in [[Test cricket]]; in the form of a small [[urn]] containing the ashes of a [[cremate]]d cricket stump or set of bails.
# {{lb|en|cricket}} A [[series]] of Test cricket matches played between England and Australia.
# {{lb|en|rugby league|sports|by extension}} A [[nominal]] trophy contested by England and Australia in other sports, especially rugby league.
# {{lb|en|rugby league|sports}} A series of such test matches.

